---
import BlogPostLayout from '../../../../layouts/BlogPostLayout.astro';

const lang = 'en-us';
const post = { title: 'Baia di Recommone', subtitle: 'The Hidden Refuge Between Nerano and Crapolla', category: 'DISCOVERIES', date: 'May 20, 2026', readTime: '10 min', image: '/images/baia-recommone-hero.jpg', imageAlt: 'Baia di Recommone with tower and beach', path: '/en-us/blog/baia-recommone/' };
const metaTitle = 'Baia di Recommone: The Hidden Refuge Between Nerano and Crapolla';
const metaDescription = 'Discover Baia di Recommone, the secret beach between Marina del Cantone and Crapolla Fjord. Aragonese tower, crystal-clear water and snorkeling: a hidden gem of the Amalfi Coast.';
const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/en-us/' },
  { name: 'Blog', url: '/en-us/blog/' },
  { name: 'Baia di Recommone', url: '/en-us/blog/baia-recommone/' },
];
const quickInfo = [
  { label: 'Departure', value: 'Marina del Cantone / Nerano' },
  { label: 'Duration', value: '15–20 min' },
  { label: 'Difficulty', value: 'Easy' },
  { label: 'Beach type', value: 'Partially free, partially equipped' },
  { label: 'Access', value: 'On foot or water taxi' },
];
const faq = [
  {
    q: 'How do I reach Baia di Recommone?',
    a: 'From Marina del Cantone in Nerano, a short 15–20 minute trail on easy terrain. Alternatively, by direct water taxi.'
  },
  {
    q: 'Is it a free beach?',
    a: 'Baia di Recommone is partially free (towards the rock) and partially equipped (with the Conca del Sogno restaurant). Both accesses are public.'
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I snorkel here?',
    a: 'Yes, the water is crystal-clear and rich in marine life (fish, octopuses, starfish). It\'s one of the best snorkeling spots on the Amalfi Coast.'
  },
  {
    q: 'Is there a freshwater spring?',
    a: 'No, but the Conca del Sogno restaurant offers water (if you dine). We recommend bringing at least 1L of water from Nerano.'
  },
  {
    q: 'What\'s the best time to visit?',
    a: 'May–September. June is ideal: perfect sun and not yet crowded. July-August is beautiful but packed with tourists.'
  },
];
const sidebarLinks = [
  { label: 'Amalfi Coast', href: '/en-us/amalfi-coast/' },
  { label: 'Marina del Cantone', href: '/en-us/beaches/sorrentine-peninsula/marina-del-cantone/' },
  { label: 'Crapolla Fjord', href: '/en-us/blog/fiordo-di-crapolla/' },
  { label: 'Punta Campanella', href: '/en-us/blog/punta-campanella/' },
];
const authorRole = 'Travel Specialist & Coastal Expert';
const relatedArticles = [
  { title: 'Crapolla Fjord: The 700 Steps Between Myth and Wild Nature', href: '/en-us/blog/fiordo-di-crapolla/', category: 'DISCOVERIES', image: '/images/fiordo-crapolla-hero.jpg' },
  { title: 'Punta Campanella: Where Legend Meets Nature', href: '/en-us/blog/punta-campanella/', category: 'DISCOVERIES', image: '/images/punta-campanella-hero.jpg' },
  { title: 'Trekking & Path of the Gods', href: '/en-us/experiences/trekking/', category: 'EXPERIENCES', image: '/images/trekking-hero.jpg' },
];
const keyTakeaways = [
  'Baia di Recommone is the hidden gem between Nerano and Crapolla: 15 minutes on foot from Marina del Cantone, completely isolated from mass tourism.',
  'The water is extraordinarily transparent and rich in marine life, making it one of the best snorkeling spots on the Amalfi Coast.',
  'The Recommone Tower (15th century) dominates the bay and offers stunning views of the Galli Archipelago.',
  'Dual access: free beach towards the rock or the Conca del Sogno restaurant with loungers and services.',
  'Perfect for those seeking tranquility, snorkeling and wild landscapes, without crowds of tourists.'
];
const videoSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "VideoObject",
  "name": "Baia di Recommone: The Hidden Refuge Between Nerano and Crapolla",
  "description": "Discover Baia di Recommone, the secret beach between Marina del Cantone and Crapolla Fjord. Crystal-clear water, Aragonese tower and spectacular snorkeling.",
  "thumbnailUrl": "/images/baia-recommone-hero.jpg",
  "uploadDate": "2026-05-20",
  "duration": "PT2M15S",
  "contentUrl": "/videos/baia-recommone-video.mp4",
  "videoDetails": {
    "width": "1280",
    "height": "720"
  }
};
---

<BlogPostLayout lang={lang} post={post} metaTitle={metaTitle} metaDescription={metaDescription} breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs} quickInfo={quickInfo} faq={faq} sidebarLinks={sidebarLinks} authorRole={authorRole} relatedArticles={relatedArticles} schema={[videoSchema]} pageKey="baia-recommone">

  <div class="space-y-6">
    <p class="text-lg text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
      Between Marina del Cantone (Nerano) and Crapolla Fjord exists a bay that seems stolen from geography: a crescent of sand and rock where the water is so transparent you can see fish as if they were in an aquarium. It's called Baia di Recommone, and it's the secret refuge that savvy Amalfi Coast travelers guard jealously. It's not the easiest to reach (but not complicated either), and it's partially equipped with an exclusive restaurant. For this reason, it miraculously remains peaceful even in August.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="rounded-[2rem] shadow-xl mb-8 flex justify-center bg-slate-900 py-4">
    <video controls poster="/images/baia-recommone-hero.jpg" class="max-w-full max-h-[500px]" width="1280" height="720">
      <source src="/videos/baia-recommone-video.mp4?v=2" type="video/mp4" />
      Your browser does not support the video tag. Please update your browser to view the video.
    </video>
    <script>
      const video = document.getElementById("disable-audio");
      if (!video) video = document.querySelector('video');
      if (video) {
        const forceMuted = () => {
          video.muted = true;
          video.volume = 0;
        };
        forceMuted();
        video.addEventListener('play', forceMuted);
        video.addEventListener('playing', forceMuted);
        video.addEventListener('volumechange', forceMuted);
        video.addEventListener('timeupdate', forceMuted);
        video.addEventListener('seeked', forceMuted);
      }
    </script>
  </div>

  <section class="space-y-6">
    <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900">The Scenic Trail: From Nerano to Recommone</h2>

    <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
      The true magic of Baia di Recommone begins with the trail that connects it to Marina del Cantone. It's a mere 15–20 minute walk, almost entirely downhill, with views over the sea increasing at every step. The trail is well-marked and very easy: perfect for those who don't enjoy exhausting hikes, but want to experience a wild beach.
    </p>

    <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Recommone Tower: The Aragonese Guard of the Galli</h3>
    <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
      Dominating the bay stands the Recommone Tower, a perfect example of 15th-century defensive architecture. Built by the Aragonese to protect the coast from Barbary pirate attacks, today it is a silent monument watching over the Galli Archipelago. From its base, the views are spectacular: the Faraglioni of Li Galli stand out on the horizon, while the Amalfi Coast fades into the distance. It's one of those moments when you understand why the ancients built fortresses in these places.
    </p>

    <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">The Fishermen's Grotto: Natural Shelter and Boat Sanctuary</h3>
    <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
      Hidden among the bay's rocks is a natural cave that for centuries was used by local fishermen as shelter and a boat repository. Today it's a public space, a natural refuge where you can rest in the shade during the hottest hours of the day. The water around the grotto is particularly rich in marine life, making it a perfect oasis for snorkeling.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-6">
    <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900">Water Worthy of an Oscar</h2>

    <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
      If there's a parameter that defines the quality of a Mediterranean beach, it's water transparency. Baia di Recommone is one of the very few places on the Amalfi Coast where you can see the bottom at 3–4 meters deep. The water is so crystal-clear that the first impact is almost overwhelming. The bay is naturally protected from waves thanks to the rock formation, which means it's calm even when the sea outside is rough.
    </p>

    <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
      For snorkeling enthusiasts, this is a sort of earthly paradise. Just meters from the shore swim fish of various sizes, curious octopuses emerging from their lairs, orange and purple starfish. It's not rare to see the occasional moray eel (always peaceful) or sea urchins. It's intimate and safe snorkeling, perfect for beginners and families.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-6">
    <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900">Technical Information</h2>

    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full border-collapse border border-slate-300">
        <tbody>
          <tr class="bg-slate-50">
            <td class="border border-slate-300 px-4 py-2 font-semibold text-slate-900">Departure</td>
            <td class="border border-slate-300 px-4 py-2 text-slate-700">Marina del Cantone / Nerano (via trail or water taxi)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="border border-slate-300 px-4 py-2 font-semibold text-slate-900">Duration</td>
            <td class="border border-slate-300 px-4 py-2 text-slate-700">15–20 minutes (on foot)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="bg-slate-50">
            <td class="border border-slate-300 px-4 py-2 font-semibold text-slate-900">Difficulty</td>
            <td class="border border-slate-300 px-4 py-2 text-slate-700">Easy</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="border border-slate-300 px-4 py-2 font-semibold text-slate-900">Beach type</td>
            <td class="border border-slate-300 px-4 py-2 text-slate-700">Wild beach (free section), Conca del Sogno (equipped section with restaurant)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="bg-slate-50">
            <td class="border border-slate-300 px-4 py-2 font-semibold text-slate-900">Water access</td>
            <td class="border border-slate-300 px-4 py-2 text-slate-700">On foot (trail) or water taxi from Marina del Cantone</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="border border-slate-300 px-4 py-2 font-semibold text-slate-900">Services</td>
            <td class="border border-slate-300 px-4 py-2 text-slate-700">Conca del Sogno restaurant (for loungers and food), otherwise complete freedom</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="bg-slate-50">
            <td class="border border-slate-300 px-4 py-2 font-semibold text-slate-900">Best period</td>
            <td class="border border-slate-300 px-4 py-2 text-slate-700">May–September; ideal June (perfect sun, still peaceful)</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-6">
    <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900">Expert Tips</h2>

    <div class="space-y-4">
      <div class="border-l-4 border-med-gold bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-r-lg">
        <h4 class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">Choose your access based on the vibe you want</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-700 text-sm">Want wild beach? Access from the rock side (completely free). Want comfort and food? The Conca del Sogno restaurant offers loungers, umbrellas and cuisine (reservation recommended). Both accesses intersect, so you can combine them.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="border-l-4 border-med-blue bg-charcoal p-4 rounded-r-lg">
        <h4 class="font-semibold text-white mb-2">Take a water taxi if you don't want to walk</h4>
        <p class="text-white/80 text-sm">If the trail doesn't appeal, Marina del Cantone has water taxis that depart directly to Recommone. Costs ~€10–15 per person, but you save the trek and can carry more luggage.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="border-l-4 border-med-gold bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-r-lg">
        <h4 class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">Plan for the sun: morning is better</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-700 text-sm">Baia di Recommone receives direct sun from about 9:00 AM to 3:30 PM. After 3:30 PM the rock's shadow covers much of the beach. Tip: arrive between 10:00 and 11:00 AM to maximize sun time.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="border-l-4 border-med-blue bg-charcoal p-4 rounded-r-lg">
        <h4 class="font-semibold text-white mb-2">Bring snorkeling gear</h4>
        <p class="text-white/80 text-sm">Even just a pair of fins and a mask make a difference. For a complete experience, bring a snorkel and an underwater camera (the snorkeling here is truly spectacular).</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-slate-50 rounded-lg p-6 space-y-4">
    <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Key Takeaways</h3>
    <ul class="space-y-2">
      {keyTakeaways.map((item) => (
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
          <span class="text-med-gold font-bold text-xl flex-shrink-0">→</span>
          <span class="text-slate-700">{item}</span>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </section>

</BlogPostLayout>
